764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-124087/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124087" :question/id #uuid "a5033c15-e0ed-52f4-b026-2ec54fd36d33" :question/math-academy-id "q-124087" :question/problem "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - ${\\sum }_{n=100}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent\nII. - $-{10}^{10}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=100}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}-{10}^{10}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the properties of convergent series:\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }K\\cdot {a}_{n}=K\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Removing a finite number of terms from a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement II is true. Any constant multiple of a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement III is true. The sum of two convergent series is convergent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124087/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d138d2c-3295-5eae-990d-42711f5792f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124087"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123754/answer/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64" :answer/id #uuid "6b56962b-255e-51b5-8b0e-4c1c7dd1a168" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123754/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "8884e2e3-45f2-59ba-a7ec-06e8f55db610" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-123754/answer/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64" :answer-field/choices ["q-123754/answer/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123754" :question/id #uuid "c56dbdf4-b093-5a0b-896e-fd12c3e29f0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-123754" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=t-4,\\,\\,\\,y=1-2{t}^{2},\\,0\\le t\\le 4,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $a$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $b$ | $c$ | $-31$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=t-4.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=0-4=-4.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=1-2{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=1-2(2)^{2}=-7.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=1-2{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=1-2(3)^{2}=-17\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-4+(-7)+(-17)=-28.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123754/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123754"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-6832/answer/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "d07a408d-61e2-5c18-ae4f-c310d6a3fc68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6832/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "757137c4-df81-5d0c-9722-1fd017aa21a9" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-6832/answer/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-6832/answer/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-6832" :question/id #uuid "bb6b00ad-d0da-51b8-947a-ae3a849534d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-6832" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}),\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}),\\,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0$ | $b$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $a$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $-a+b+c.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $y=\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\na=\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{\\pi (-3)}{3})=\\operatorname{cos}(-\\pi )=-1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi (-1)}{2})=\\operatorname{sin}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi (3)}{2})=\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n-a+b+c=-(-1)+(-1)+(-1)=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-6832/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-6832"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69923/answer/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "8fc224f3-876f-5816-892b-79717b173126" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69923/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "29e41ae2-ae31-55b2-8633-b421b7bdd207" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-69923/answer/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-69923/answer/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-69923" :question/id #uuid "97d679c9-1cde-5a51-924a-06ae37ba6ab4" :question/math-academy-id "q-69923" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=-3t,\\,\\,\\,y=2t,\\,-5\\le t\\le 0,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-5$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $15$ | $12$ | $9$ | $6$ | $3$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $-10$ | $a$ | $-6$ | $b$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a-b+c.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-4$ into $y=2t.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=2(-4)=-8.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into $y=2t.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=2(-2)-4.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=-3t.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=-3(0)=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na-b+c=-8-(-4)+0=-4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-69923/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69923"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-326248/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "2444c709-d123-5806-a9dd-efcb4142d7c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answ