87e6b27d26252dee3574ece2f6ad977f5921545" "q-152912/selection/d6f99be275c26eb6718cffc223484405f7c8a0a15bdc1ead58e8b620780a74dd" "q-152912/selection/d5891d7bb537be3b6a2959769e791056b9cfadb879b2cff25bb856176f87fe11" "q-152912/selection/e3d2fe88e0a6276340259e92299bc642235399ae984bcd5c01683ba96b78879e" "q-152912/selection/e15fb346f1cc4a29beac92a2d960de479c0b5bb32e566062fcb888a0c1370f7f" "q-152912/selection/12c9f2bc4b37d922f1e1e27a337281708a41d8fd76808ee759fa36b24d369e80" "q-152912/selection/f34e4a361c82d3d038fc4d03ac7649411abbb66628aa61700fe97ab48fa8810f" "q-152912/selection/9d869808e53a23386bbcec29e7c70dcf2a3a3621d5ff5dccf72ada0187b39692" "q-152912/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-152912" :question/id #uuid "02eda226-1684-50b8-a1ed-83b979a1c53a" :question/math-academy-id "q-152912" :question/problem "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-x-3, & x<-3 \\\\ 0, & x=-3 \\\\ x+3, & x>-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\nI. - $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-3$\nII. - ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}f(x)$\nIII. - ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}f(x)=f(-3)$\nIV. - $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-3$" :question/worked-solution "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n- Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Using the expression for the second branch of the function, we obtain that\n\n$$\nf(-3)=0.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-3.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is true. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}(-x-3) \\\\  & =-(-3)-3 \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}(x+3) \\\\  & =(-3)+3 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=-3$ exists:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)}f(x)=0\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have that ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}f(x)=0=f(-3).$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since all statements I-III are true, according to the continuity test, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All the statements are true.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-152912/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8edb0a6c-f22f-56cf-9545-2fae93896db2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-152912"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-152928/selection/cc54ccae9ecbe61a650173303111652be25e358bea2c6fc89973c699ac869f66" :answer/id #uuid "3ba37a39-4d97-5b49-8d13-91ee55115a42" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152928/selection/4ca814a26a9344b418765bf1216091351959544cfa5933e8f718fbb4daf8fcd7" :answer/id #uuid "5fdaa303-0c0b-5b4e-823f-edbaf5152f63" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152928/selection/e1b08c30ae6409d86384e6d45f16261c1030a9c86db05f53c8c675e9c30c4980" :answer/id #uuid "c6d5aea5-3dfa-517c-a044-6c722ffa4a07" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152928/selection/6cef23069c284027c89d195df9fea27427e9a7779aa03b92f69bdc30aa1481f3" :answer/id #uuid "f38c8c38-23aa-5d68-b966-e6c20ea1a14c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152928/selection/5b0d2458ae733823dd831903d956623078e5a9515cb620d43842b7efd3eee3ad" :answer/id #uuid "f37ad898-cae0-5dd0-aa72-3e95cd65fde5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-152928/selection/5aab6e99e2d2fe7023a3e69c393d3f70