c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118782" :question/id #uuid "c6fe84cb-75e2-55de-b6df-ded3330a421e" :question/math-academy-id "q-118782" :question/problem "Which of the following are second-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nI. - $9x{y}^{''}+8{y}^{'}=4$\nII. - $\\sqrt{{y}^{''}+x}=3y$\nIII. - ${y}^{‴}+{x}^{2}{y}^{''}=3$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of second-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{''}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''}.$\n\n- Equation II is also a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''}.$\n\n- Equation III is not a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-118782/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "443c0bd0-2e77-50a8-91d3-a288d4ee852b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118782"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118780/answer/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "5ca617c8-ae0c-50ae-9246-ed19fda55c63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118780/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "42064ebd-20a9-5478-a842-ced33dee8f82" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-118780/answer/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-118780/answer/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118780" :question/id #uuid "6548405c-a613-5075-b99b-e7774982d1db" :question/math-academy-id "q-118780" :question/problem "What is the order of the ordinary differential equation ${x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{7}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{7}}-9{x}^{7}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{8}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{8}}?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{8}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{8}},$ which has order $8.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118780/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "443c0bd0-2e77-50a8-91d3-a288d4ee852b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118780"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-96702/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "d24cd77e-16ed-5f5a-9c5e-0234683e143e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96702/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "06e6c92a-97d1-564d-863d-bda507afccfd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96702/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "c2d72649-3668-5f78-ada6-9565b30f7fe3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96702/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "dd234ff3-f83e-5cf9-87fe-e14c16f76f18" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96702/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "e07ee293-119a-578f-9cb9-bdb3e5415610" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96702/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f8784524-b57e-5054-9fa6-028c173f4c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96702/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "af8323ab-ddb1-5f48-a9f7-f5692ae339da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96702/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "a2cfd61a-0a0f-5f14-900b-5550cae3912a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96702/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f7fab41-ea7c-53fd-85ac-6541129d2e5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-96702/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-96702/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-96702/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-96702/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-96702/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-96702/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-96702/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-96702/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-96702/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-96702" :question/id #uuid "6d484918-7854-547b-b753-257beeb0c7d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-96702" :question/problem "Which of the following are autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\nI. - $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x={e}^{y}$\nII. - $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2=\\sqrt{y}$\nIII. - $4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{x}{y}=5y$" :question/worked-solution "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{'}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation I is not an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x & ={e}^{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{y}+x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)={e}^{y}+x.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).$\n\n- Equation II is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2 & =\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{y}+2}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=\\frac{\\sqrt{y}+2}{2}.$\n\n- Equation III is not an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{x}{y} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{4}(5y+\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{4}(5y+\\frac{x}{y}).$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-96702/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fa0c4b2-8dc6-5823-a9bb-b933a9f9ee7f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96702"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-96712/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c053f2d6-9364-55b3-954f-91552728a08d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96712/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "9e078445-c2fc-5a31-88ab-c2be941bd0f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96712/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "8163967d-e6d8-56ce-9dca-756d234c3020" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96712/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "11bda8cf-ada4-544f-8e86-30b984916eaa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96712/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "be9955de-2d2b-52bd-ad19-a9c11284301d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96712/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "31036b5b-7449-5599-8b7f-8b39b778f239" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96712/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "60ed9cbb-4ba4-51aa-a0f8-7225e1688c36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96712/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "f1a652c4-ff96-5e6d-b026-86d6eed744a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96712/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "831ff5c2-b840-5fe4-b6ea-ec995d5e6729" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-96712/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-96712/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-96712/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-96712/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-96712/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-96712/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-96712/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-96712/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-96712/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-96712" :question/id #uuid "a6f5f12c-8742-57e1-8431-b7e5f7c8b33f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96712" :question/problem "Which of the following are **not** autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\nI. - ${y}^{'}=1-\\sqrt{y}$\nII. - ${y}^{'}-\\operatorname{tan}y={e}^{2}$\nIII. - $x{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{y}=4$" :question/worked-solution "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{'}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation I is an autonomous differential equation. It is of the form ${y}^{'}=f(y),$ where $f(y)=1-\\sqrt{y}.$\n\n- Equation II is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form ${y}^{'}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{'}-\\operatorname{tan}y & ={e}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{'} & =\\operatorname{tan}y+{e}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{'} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=\\operatorname{tan}y+{e}^{2}.$\n\n- Equation III is *not* an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{y} & =4 \\\\ {y}^{'} & =\\frac{4y+1}{xy} \\\\ {y}^{'} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)=\\frac{4y+1}{xy}.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form ${y}^{'}=f(y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-96712/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fa0c4b2-8dc6-5823-a9bb-b933a9f9ee7f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96712"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-96992/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f0377b83-e245-52ea-80a0-298ddfe36899" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96992/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f1223c20-84d2-5fb5-bf8a-545a08f3d710" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96992/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "c6bcccdb-85b9-52d9-b7ca-5d988b9f7fb5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96992/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "070e48b3-a56e-5c40-9343-941d4858140e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96992/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "e20c0aff-74cc-552d-96eb-eef3a81e96ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96992/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "6cee0851-d168-5175-af4b-4e9ec6593fd0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96992/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "491c18dc-e9d5-5a2b-88f5-a3bc86a065ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96992/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "40d7f3bf-ff28-581c-96a7-f1b98edbccd3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96992/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "36b80bee-db64-535d-aace-058b279199ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-96992/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-96992/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-96992/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-96992/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-96992/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-96992/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-96992/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-96992/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-96992/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-96992" :question/id #uuid "f324e71f-0765-5434-b640-0e2263e787be" :question/math-academy-id "q-96992" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nI. - $3{x}^{2}{y}^{'}={y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1$\nII. - $\\frac{{y}^{'}}{2}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}=y,\\,y(1)=2$\nIII. - ${y}^{'}-x\\sqrt{y}={e}^{x}$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{'}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System I is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $3{x}^{2}{y}^{'}={y}^{2}$ together with the initial condition $y(0)=1.$\n\n- System II is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $\\frac{{y}^{'}}{2}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}=y$ together with the initial condition $y(1)=2.$\n\n- System III  is not a first-order initial value problem. We have a first-order ordinary differential equation, but there is no initial condition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-96992/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96992"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118786/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "3dac5233-1cb8-538b-a95f-9c3184be17d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118786/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d2471a44-b1ef-5141-9fe5-a87c669720c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118786/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "c9953a88-e46e-55ac-b3c0-ab066edb021f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/vali