b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-118786/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-118786/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118786" :question/id #uuid "7d3e1743-cd34-559d-bad0-d34093686fd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-118786" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nI. - $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{'}=8y,\\,y(-1)=3$\nII. - $8{y}^{'}-xy=3$\nIII. - $3{y}^{''}=4y,\\,y(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{'}(-1)=1$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{'}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System I is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{'}=8y$ together with the initial condition $y(-1)=3.$\n\n- System II is not a first-order initial value problem. We have a first-order ordinary differential equation, but there is no initial condition.\n\n- System III is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation $3{y}^{''}=4y$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{'}(-1)=1.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118786/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118786"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47778/answer/98bafb703e8881681adce0bc8183cfd2e95c4591cd3a7132eb4a51d89a40e205" :answer/id #uuid "6574fd45-455a-5ce6-8ad8-68abbf105320" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All real numbers" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47778/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "82c34cd0-ab73-5aef-b587-d37f07c81adf" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-47778/answer/98bafb703e8881681adce0bc8183cfd2e95c4591cd3a7132eb4a51d89a40e205" :answer-field/choices ["q-47778/answer/98bafb703e8881681adce0bc8183cfd2e95c4591cd3a7132eb4a51d89a40e205"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47778" :question/id #uuid "f7b6a962-a925-5eb4-8eb3-c093275b7ef1" :question/math-academy-id "q-47778" :question/problem "What's the range of $f(x)={log}_{9}x?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}\n\nUse an interval in words, such as \"All real numbers\"." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{9}x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/40664f83ba162a93ed06970798d37798db90b85c21d44a9ed20f338df4e1b4e1.png)\n\nThe domain of $y={log}_{9}x$ is $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ and the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All real numbers.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47778/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5468f23-98bd-52d9-ba21-85e5eea058a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47778"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-156739/answer/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" :answer/id #uuid "e2a3223c-8742-53bd-8709-f6c1553158e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156739/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "989bc62c-f1d9-568f-95a9-4796196afea2" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-156739/answer/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" :answer-field/choices ["q-156739/answer/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-156739" :question/id #uuid "bc9adfeb-d883-541f-9bc6-0ae368d34338" :question/math-academy-id "q-156739" :question/problem "What is a horizontal asymptote of $y={log}_{8}x?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}\n\nIf none exist, enter a phrase such as \"No horizontal asymptotes\"." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{8}x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/c9bc40573836e39bfb5c9ea0dab41b66ba7bb753bc7580936a3eb206b968e5c1.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note that for $x>1$, the graph grows very slowly as we increase $x.$ \n\nWe say that $y\\to \\infty $ (slowly) as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, there are no horizontal asymptotes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-156739/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06ede1c9-b17d-504b-86a8-9284f7ded093"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-156739"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-156741/answer/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" :answer/id #uuid "a943c892-3b5f-5717-b297-77d4278d417c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No horizontal asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156741/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "a156b458-fd69-567e-be85-623822c9cfeb" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-156741/answer/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843" :answer-field/choices ["q-156741/answer/3e622b14fb9e8408568d99d85f4dbc69d704ea59c7efa30ae415e06682e77843"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-156741" :question/id #uuid "d0452204-fefa-5ed6-b9ea-ca7949b58b72" :question/math-academy-id "q-156741" :question/problem "What is a horizontal asymptote of $y={log}_{6}x?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}\n\nIf none exist, enter a phrase such as \"No horizontal asymptotes\"." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{6}x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/4177d9520b3758b29926eba7a7a74ed4c508d861e3c343f46c372ec79500fc9d.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note that for $x>1$, the graph grows very slowly as we increase $x.$ \n\nWe say that $y\\to \\infty $ (slowly) as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, there are no horizontal asymptotes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-156741/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06ede1c9-b17d-504b-86a8-9284f7ded093"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-156741"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-156743/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "eaba9b1d-0fae-50cc-8ec8-d77adfa6a6e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156743/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "97f00078-2a9c-54b8-9d9b-3822a0e5f9af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156743/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e9be5aba-533d-57b5-a4e7-92b37a03a4c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156743/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "ddd04498-e892-5b43-8f3d-83b52b4c10c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156743/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "4c7e53ce-1bbd-56fe-958e-a730dc197ffa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "