ion $y={log}_{6}x?$ \n\nI. - It has no zeros\nII. - $y\\to 6$ as $x\\to \\infty $\nIII. - It has a vertical asymptote at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y={log}_{6}x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/d8d3f9dc995d8801d451b15129860362efa772178cdc3ef07be5adb6a1da5c45.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a zero at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As $x$ increases, $y$ increases without bound. Therefore, $y\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty $\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-156743/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f1fce29-a071-5a86-8a5e-0e7093558d0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-156743"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69791/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "40e36838-8b21-54b1-8762-5ad5ccff12d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69791/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "5162764c-a93f-5b9a-bd1e-2e9c26b3a693" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69791/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d660b1d0-8f74-5e2a-95a1-a3d4bfbb381a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69791/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "722f8723-5569-5bf5-9c17-5140e64ebe19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69791/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "77a8eadb-a898-5c1c-ab62-f63855a24e95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69791/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "c402868e-47ed-50be-b9a7-189ca376d7a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69791/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "75311fce-4feb-567e-b92c-49d719962b96" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69791/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "f7bd8e97-4a84-5829-9d91-27806062c05c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69791/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b376239-9277-5a5a-b27c-bad904bb69b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-69791/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-69791/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-69791/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-69791/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-69791/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-69791/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-69791/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-69791/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-69791/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-69791" :question/id #uuid "22db072b-47e0-5531-be05-96bd3329aa8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-69791" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y={log}_{5}x?$\n\nI. - The domain is $x>1$\nII. - It has a maximum at $x=1$\nIII. - It passes through the point $(25,2)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y={log}_{5}x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/fd8c4765fa1b07d58a4d0b2e90a07383f5475883a2ada747ea6ae32e7a73808b.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the graph, we see that the domain is $x>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is strictly increasing on its entire domain. Therefore, there are no maximum values.\n\n- Statement III is true. Substituting $x=25$ into the equation of the curve gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={log}_{5}(25) \\\\  & ={log}_{5}({5}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\,\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-69791/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f1fce29-a071-5a86-8a5e-0e7093558d0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69791"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9908/answer/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "8d4fd620-0900-55af-8837-e928f5f4ee8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9908/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "150d451a-00ce-5a55-8435-8e6fa936af48" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-9908/answer/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-9908/answer/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9908" :question/id #uuid "c1aeb34a-99a8-5372-b85e-e163f31127c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-9908" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}x},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $y$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{cos}x$ and $v(x)=1+\\operatorname{sin}x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}x)^{'}\\cdot (1+\\operatorname{sin}x)-\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot (1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{'}}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}x)(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)-(\\operatorname{cos}x)\\operatorname{cos}x}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}x-{sin}^{2}x-{cos}^{2}x)}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}x-({sin}^{2}x+{cos}^{2}x))}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Since ${sin}^{2}x+{cos}^{2}x=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}x-1)}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)}{(1+\\operatorname{sin}x)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{sin}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $-\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-9908/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c547746-49c8-5a4a-85fe-c6b75493a354"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9908"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319825/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "48cf976f-c492-5116-a478-b5c3d499c7bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319825/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c4079ac-5969-5352-90bf-234b527c5450" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319825/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-319825/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319825" :question/id #uuid "dd0e54ab-23dd-5fbf-99e4-afe94b73a3d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-319825" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(x-1)\\operatorname{ln}(2x+1),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=0$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=x-1$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}(2x+1).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(x-1)\\cdot \\frac{2}{2x+1}+\\operatorname{ln}(2x+1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x-1)}{2x+1}+\\operatorname{ln}(2x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=0$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{2(0-1)}{2(0)+1}+\\operatorname{ln}(2(0)+1) \\\\  & =(-2)+\\operatorname{ln}(1) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-319825/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee64135e-9b9f-5429-a4df-efa522042b83"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319825"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70210/answer/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b700da5e-ba2d-5a12-ab05-324fb4f0bdd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70210/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc3f2cd-a3d6-5ac2-af86-a346aff71d9e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-70210/answer/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-70210/answer/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70210" :question/id #uuid "cb756b6f-c9b7-51dc-82e2-024fa8b2534a" :question/math-academy-id "q-70210" :question/problem "If you deposit $$2,000$ into an account with a $20%$ annual interest rate, compounded semi-annually, how many years will it take until there is at least $$4,000$ in the account?\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The compound interest equation states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & ={P}_{0}{(1+\\frac{r}{n})}^{nt}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe annual interest is compounded semi-annually, so $n=2.$ We also have an initial amount of ${P}_{0}=2,000$ and annual rate of $r=0.2.$\n\nTo find the number of years it will take until $P\\ge 4,000,$ we substitute these values into the formula and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P={P}_{0}{(1+\\frac{r}{n})}^{nt} & \\ge 4,000 \\\\ 2,000{(1+\\frac{0.2}{2})}^{2t} & \\ge 4,000 \\\\ (1+0.1)^{2t} & \\ge \\frac{4,000}{2,000} \\\\ (1.1)^{2t} & \\ge 2 \\\\ \\operatorname{log}({1.1}^{2t}) & \\ge \\operatorname{log}(2) \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{log}(1.1) & \\ge \\operatorname{log}(2) \\\\ 2t & \\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{log}(2)}{\\operatorname{log}(1.1)} \\\\ 2t & \\ge 7.272… \\\\ t & \\ge \\frac{7.272…}{2}\\approx 3.64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemember payments are compounded semi-annually, so we must choose either $3.5$ or $4$ years.\n\n- After $3.5$ years, there is still less than $$4,000$ in the account, because $3.5<3.64.$\n\n- After $4$ years, there will be more than $$4,000$ in the account, since $4>3.64.$\n\nTherefore, it will take $4$ years until there is at least $$4,000$ in the account." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-70210/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c88884a-128a-5d46-bfbe-3773139ee11c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70210"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-166947/answer/23c4d9cdccc3b0bd9ea06a9eb5dde58b720ceae45d6141c2b790a41f11744e08" :answer/id #uuid "36592917-0e89-59ea-b1c9-ec6fac2a0b0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-166947/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "0158252f-0174-5ffd-92f6-829d16529201" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-166947/answer/23c4d9cdccc3b0bd9ea06a9eb5dde58b720ceae45d6141c2b790a41f11744e08" :answer-field/choices ["q-166947/answer/23c4d9cdccc3b0bd9ea06a9eb5dde58b720ceae45d6141c2b790a41f11744e08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-166947" :question/id #uuid "c960aee5-3c8c-5166-a2ed-4e95f0b23d9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-166947" :question/problem "If you deposit $$12,000$ into an account with a $8%$ annual interest rate, compounded quarterly, how many years will it take until there is at least $$18,000$ in the account?\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The compound interest equation states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & ={P}_{0}{(1+\\frac{r}{n})}^{nt}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe annual interest is compounded quarterly, and there are $4$ quarters in one year, so $n=4.$ We also have an initial amount of ${P}_{0}=12,000$ and annual rate of $r=0.08.$\n\nTo find the number of years it will take until $P\\ge 18,000,$ we substitute these values into the formula and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P={P}_{0}{(1+\\frac{r}{n})}^{nt} & \\ge 18,000 \\\\ 12,000{(1+\\frac{0.08}{4})}^{4t} & \\ge 18,000 \\\\ (1+0.02)^{4t} & \\ge \\frac{18,000}{12,000} \\\\ (1.02)^{4t} & \\ge 1.5 \\\\ log\\,({1.02}^{4t}) & \\ge log\\,(1.5) \\\\ 4tlog\\,(1.02) & \\ge log\\,(1.5) \\\\ 4t & \\ge \\frac{log\\,(1.5)}{log\\,(1.02)} \\\\ 4t & \\ge 20.475… \\\\ t & \\ge \\frac{20.475…}{4}\\approx 5.12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemember, payments are compounded quarterly, so we must choose either $5$ or $5.25$ years.\n\n- After $5$ years, there is still less than $$18,000$ in the account, because $5<5.12.$\n\n- After $5.25$ years, there will be more than $$18,000$ in the account, since $5.25>5.12.$\n\nTherefore, it will take $5.25$ years ($5$ years and $1$ quarter) until there is at least $$18,000$ in the account." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-166947/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c88884a-128a-5d46-bfbe-3773139ee11c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-166947"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125241/answer/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "9223958e-a313-563a-b01a-410817ff2f1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125241/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5648d9c-3272-5b32-a9f7-d1439002ed53" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-125241/answer/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer-field/choices ["q-125241/answer/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125241" :question/id #uuid "0cf29daa-b0e5-53b9-baa2-725e5b094a4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-125241" :question/problem "Use the $p$-test to determine whether the series below converges or diverges.\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{{n}^{9}}\n$$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The series can be written as\n\n$$\n18{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{9}}.\n$$\n\nThis is a $p$-series with $p=9.$ Since $p>1,$ the series is convergent.\n\nNote that the factor of $18$ multiplying the series has no effect on the convergence/divergence of the series." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125241/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ead28b84-1f92-510d-87b3-07eb9a394622"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125241"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81428/answer/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "fdf7ece4-2637-5e3a-b02a-bb98b44fc983" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81428/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "38656401-8add-54f7-bee5-27e9e0e46e34" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-81428/answer/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-81428/answer/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81428" :question/id #uuid "cf874b53-ef0a-5fdf-9ef3-0a8f809bc7de" :question/math-academy-id "q-81428" :question/problem "Use the $p$-test to determine whether the series below converges or diverges.\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{n}\n$$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The series can be written as\n\n$$\n8{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{n}.\n$$\n\nThis is a $p$-series with $p=1$ (the harmonic series). Since $p\\le 1,$ the series is divergent.\n\nNote that the factor of $8$ multiplying the series has no effect on the convergence/divergence of the series." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81428/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ead28b84-1f92-510d-87b3-07eb9a394622"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81428"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9334/answer/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "f434f7ee-2d39-5a22-9c70-41bd16dc432f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9334/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "bccb7fea-91f1-5488-9cfc-3f870d14529a" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-9334/answer/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-9334/answer/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9334" :question/id #uuid "47306eda-69a1-5c4c-86bf-6d6e220f28a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-9334" :question/problem "Determine whether the series\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}}$\nconverges or diverges.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The series can be written as\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{3/2}},\n$$\n\nwhich is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Since $p>1$, the series is convergent. \n\nNote that the factor of $3$ multiplying the series has no effect on the convergence/divergence of the series." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-9334/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "855a9c5c-9d01-584b-9b24-99834365b732"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9334"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9332/answer/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "ce94ff1f-e592-5911-a4d8-01d6f5dd50dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9332/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "801ab594-17cd-508c-b3db-45ed4c7ea1d1" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-9332/answer/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-9332/answer/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9332" :question/id #uuid "e09514d4-1e05-5fb3-ba5a-f0e56cf060c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-9332" :question/problem "Determine whether the series\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt[8]{{n}^{7}}}$\nconverges or diverges.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The series can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{7/8}},\n$$\n\nwhich is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{7}{8}.$ Since $p\\le 1$, the series is divergent. \n\nNote that the factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ multiplying the series has no effect on the convergence/divergence of the series." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-9332/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "855a9c5c-9d01-584b-9b24-99834365b732"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9332"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-50629/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b0008a49-cef9-5b3e-8b9e-c5f691191a5e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50629/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "4a02105c-bb09-5f55-963a-149b9d550997" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50629/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "0d405ad9-1854-5b2f-ba5e-5a63f59fac5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50629/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "233a6e40-88e2-5eb9-86a7-69a846a8e298" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50629/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "ef7b6a8d-bcfe-50b3-a209-f5009fafc7bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50629/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "d17dd7b5-7079-5e55-a247-27b2c0ea73e9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50629/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "e82e0a94-0ef1-5341-a309-036af807e925" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50629/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "66bff3b0-0197-5440-8606-f7cf19285068" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50629/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f719330c-8cad-5dd6-8388-518d937a28d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50629/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-50629/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-50629/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-50629/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-50629/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-50629/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-50629/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-50629/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-50629/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50629" :question/id #uuid "a897110c-16a9-5e34-8f8f-61673b309ea9" :question/math-academy-id "q-50629" :question/problem "Which of the following series are convergent?\n\nI. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{n\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}}$\nII. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{\\sqrt[9]{{n}^{2}}}$\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}}{2{n}^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "We analyze each series in turn.\n\n- First, we look at ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{n\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}}.$ Rewriting this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{n\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{n\\cdot {n}^{3/2}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{5/2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{5}{2}.$ Since $p>1,$ the series converges by the $p$-series test.\n\n- For the second series, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{\\sqrt[9]{{n}^{2}}}=8\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2/9}},\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{2}{9}.$ Since $p\\le 1,$ the series is divergent.\n\n- For the third series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}}{2{n}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3/2}}{{n}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{1/2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Since $p\\le 1,$ the series diverges by the $p$-series test.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-50629/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6051f35-c390-57ba-8448-40f53f11c1c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50629"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83593/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b3815365-f016-5d77-9ce7-512dc1e1c99f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83593/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ceb00b21-f4d3-516a-a25b-c63f9d245980" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83593/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "cd21ecf6-cc48-56ea-bc16-ba8db7b8c72a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83593/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "906d8a92-c585-5a67-8fad-0f5a15fe64dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83593/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "4c35feee-56b7-527a-9eee-d30c114b58ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83593/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "8fabf757-29a7-5810-8ad6-bd173bea819e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83593/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "6c79b06e-20b6-545a-bf3f-4ace475d5b58" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83593/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "d22f00a5-7b8e-54b3-958e-6974ad2ff725" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83593/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa99ed83-7eac-5c53-a422-b00ad94c2731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83593/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-83593/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-83593/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-83593/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-83593/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-83593/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-83593/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-83593/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-83593/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83593" :question/id #uuid "59b096bf-4af9-5e57-941d-caa731cefc46" :question/math-academy-id "q-83593" :question/problem "Which of the following series are convergent?\n\nI. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4n}$\nII. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}\\sqrt{n}}$\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{3{n}^{5}}$" :question/worked-solution "We analyze each series in turn.\n\n- First, we look at ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4n}.$ Rewriting this series gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4n}=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{n},\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a $p$-series with $p=1$ (the harmonic series). Since $p\\le 1,$ the series is divergent.\n\n- For the second series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}\\sqrt{n}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}\\cdot {n}^{1/2}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{5/2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand this is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{5}{2}.$ Since $p>1,$ the series converges by the $p$-series test.\n\n- For the third series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{3{n}^{5}} & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{5}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand this is a $p$-series with $p=5.$ Since $p>1,$ the series converges by the $p$-series test.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83593/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6051f35-c390-57ba-8448-40f53f11c1c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83593"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10907/answer/d69f2bed8c129df3ee3d2678a1764357e0cfd6f0450f8064907eb6867dfd6a83" :answer/id #uuid "9d5f8d8b-bf63-5cc8-a242-6b35439d3217" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-116" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10907/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "ca84a72e-54ab-56a5-b51a-2a49c1154ad5" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-10907/answer/d69f2bed8c129df3ee3d2678a1764357e0cfd6f0450f8064907eb6867dfd6a83" :answer-field/choices ["q-10907/answer/d69f2bed8c129df3ee3d2678a1764357e0cfd6f0450f8064907eb6867dfd6a83"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10907" :question/id #uuid "307089e8-baf9-5482-9f9b-5553f2129d31" :question/math-academy-id "q-10907" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{''}(-1)$ if $f(x)=4{x}^{5}-3{x}^{4}.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & ={(4{x}^{5}-3{x}^{4})}^{'} &  \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4{x}^{4}-4\\cdot 3{x}^{3} \\\\  & =20{x}^{4}-12{x}^{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{''}(x) & ={(20{x}^{4}-12{x}^{3})}^{'} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 20{x}^{3}-3\\cdot 12{x}^{2} \\\\  & =80{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=-1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{''}(-1) & =80(-1)^{3}-36(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =-80-36 \\\\  & =-116.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-10907/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10907"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-157060/selection/51fd10dbedb33ad93fd55b8f7c554f5a1c68a3c598ab8e5e39bb43bf80ec7a73" :answer/id #uuid "7d42eba7-2ff3-503d-b95d-6b7eb6cdb43f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-157060/selection/2f3c1dd1bc7b5e6c12fd1a66e58ffc5b07ff34b9ca432abacf624236100c14e4" :answer/id #uuid "6fa0482b-bb1b-5a8f-8260-7563e97283f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-157060/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1e69e2-802e-563b-bdb3-25096f2cfd9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-157060/selection/51fd10dbedb33ad93fd55b8f7c554f5a1c68a3c598ab8e5e39bb43bf80ec7a73" :answer-field/choices ["q-157060/selection/51fd10dbedb33ad93fd55b8f7c554f5a1c68a3c598ab8e5e39bb43bf80ec7a73" "q-157060/selection/2f3c1dd1bc7b5e6c12fd1a66e58ffc5b07ff34b9ca432abacf624236100c14e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-157060" :question/id #uuid "11a1973e-aa91-5290-99cf-1bd17e28a67e" :question/math-academy-id "q-157060" :question/problem "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following is true regarding the series ${\\sum }_{n=85}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}?$" :question/worked-solution "Removing the first $k-1$ terms from a convergent series results in a convergent series.\n\nMore precisely, assume that $k\\ge 1$ is an integer. Then, we have the following:\n\n*If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.*\n\nSo, since ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, we have that ${\\sum }_{n=85}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-157060/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d74dd4ee-45f1-5ca7-ae6c-9cbb768ac636"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-157060"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-157061/selection/51fd10dbedb33ad93fd55b8f7c554f5a1c68a3c598ab8e5e39bb43bf80ec7a73" :answer/id #uuid "1f9a4799-774c-58ae-8944-640de36765c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-157061/selection/2f3c1dd1bc7b5e6c12fd1a66e58ffc5b07ff34b9ca432abacf624236100c14e4" :answer/id #uuid "9db9ea89-a83c-5057-b773-9aa10be347d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-157061/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eae1f70e-1856-5bde-9d2c-039fc97bbfad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-157061/selection/51fd10dbedb33ad93fd55b8f7c554f5a1c68a3c598ab8e5e39bb43bf80ec7a73" :answer-field/choices ["q-157061/selection/51fd10dbedb33ad93fd55b8f7c554f5a1c68a3c598ab8e5e39bb43bf80ec7a73" "q-157061/selection/2f3c1dd1bc7b5e6c12fd1a66e58ffc5b07ff34b9ca432abacf624236100c14e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-157061" :question/id #uuid "7099c532-a199-562f-8bf0-7842daffe958" :question/math-academy-id "q-157061" :question/problem "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following is true regarding the series ${\\sum }_{n=500}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}?$" :question/worked-solution "Removing the first $k-1$ terms from a convergent series results in a convergent series.\n\nMore precisely, assume that $k\\ge 1$ is an integer. Then, we have the following:\n\n*If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.*\n\nSo, since ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, we have that ${\\sum }_{n=500}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-157061/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7