\cdot {a}_{n}=K\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. The sum of two convergent series is convergent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Any constant multiple of a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement III is true. Removing a finite number of terms from a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-157096/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d138d2c-3295-5eae-990d-42711f5792f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-157096"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-157093/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "ab01aefc-b3ed-5899-adb9-4a261f91b63d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-157093/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "914e56c2-8ca9-5a35-a730-9b53b61a5911" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-157093/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "1cbe684c-081d-531b-a9d2-ba2ed90e8114" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-157093/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "75e9cf3f-f7dc-5c31-ae95-fb4f095f918d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/en