[:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-157093" :question/id #uuid "21799ec1-c57d-5a61-9e39-d42822f17b26" :question/math-academy-id "q-157093" :question/problem "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - ${\\sum }_{n=8}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent\nII. - $12\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is divergent\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=8}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+12\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is divergent" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the properties of convergent series:\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }K\\cdot {a}_{n}=K\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. Removing a finite number of terms from a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement II is false. Any constant multiple of a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement III is false. The sum of two convergent series is convergent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-157093/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d138d2c-3295-5eae-990d-42711f5792f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-157093"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-157136/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "967558d8-749b-573a-9452-5b2811814032" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensu