tion/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-143215/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-143215/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-143215/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-143215/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-143215/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-143215/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-143215/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-143215/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143215" :question/id #uuid "1b6783c3-ebe0-5273-9cb2-dc0ed4031e6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-143215" :question/problem "Given that  ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{4}^{n}}{(n!)^{2}}$ for $n\\ge 1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - $\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}\\le 1$ for all $n\\ge 1$\nII. - ${a}_{n}$ is an increasing sequence\nIII. - ${a}_{n}$ is a decreasing sequence" :question/worked-solution "Suppose the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is a positive sequence defined for $n\\ge 1,$ and that\n\n$$\nL=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- if $L\\ge 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ then ${a}_{n}$ is *increasing,* and\n\n- if $0<L\\le 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ then ${a}_{n}$ is *decreasing.*\n\nNotice that, in this case, ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{4}^{n}}{(n!)^{2}}$ is positive for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the ratio $L,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}} & =\\frac{(\\frac{{4}^{n+1}}{((n+1)!)^{2}})}{(\\frac{{4}^{n}}{(n!)^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{n+1}(n!)^{2}}{{4}^{n}((n+1)!)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{n+1}(n!)^{2}}{{4}^{n}((n+1)n!)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{n}\\cdot 4\\cdot (n!)^{2}}{{4}^{n}\\cdot (n+1)^{2}\\cdot (n!)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{4}^{n}}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{(n!)^{2}}}{\\cancel{{4}^{n}}\\cdot (n+1)^{2}\\cdot \\cancel{(n!)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(n+1)^{2}} \\\\  & \\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, whereas statement III is true. Since $0<L\\le 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ we can conclude that the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143215/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "169f59f9-ee45-5375-a22d-4906b7a09ad0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143215"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143217/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "968b1c70-b015-5c48-b573-1869a2dd4975" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143217/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "9d852a96-7a30-5d23-8d03-f302826e638f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143217/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "773829ba-691c-5578-99ea-15e910cb4322" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143217/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "07217c3b-a2dd-576c-9462-4d8745c86aac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143217/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "4ec01e9d-e1b1-5873-a02c-c01826ec3679" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143217/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d8743484