}$ is an increasing sequence\nIII. - ${a}_{n}$ is a decreasing sequence" :question/worked-solution "Suppose the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is a positive sequence defined for $n\\ge 1,$ and that\n\n$$\nL=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- if $L\\ge 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ then ${a}_{n}$ is *increasing,* and\n\n- if $0<L\\le 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ then ${a}_{n}$ is *decreasing.*\n\nNotice that, in this case, ${a}_{n}={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{n+1}$ is positive for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the ratio $L,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{n+2}}{{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{n+1}} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{n+2-n-1} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4}{5})}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & \\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, whereas statement III is true. Since $0<L\\le 1$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ we can conclude that the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143217/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11d7e9b2-b321-5c29-992a-775750c570f0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143217"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143220/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "816d8401-ff89-562c-ae81-7b16d2a5bfcf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143220/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d2a2de85-3c1d-53ef-b1a4-3dca83582c5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143220/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "323b0993-1575-5b72-888c-f46d1ee98748" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/e