n has only irrational solutions." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $a=\\frac{1}{4},$ $b=3,$ and $c=5.$ So, we calculate the discriminant as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & =(3)^{2}-4(\\frac{1}{4})(5) \\\\  & =9-5 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd $4={2}^{2}$ is a perfect square.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. \n\nFirst, notice that our quadratic equation has rational coefficients. And, since the discriminant is a nonzero perfect square, the equation must have two rational solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-157982/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "adc75098-5640-5e81-a0bc-003fa20c090c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-157982"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158002/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "31acbb2d-ad20-5b0f-963a-864f1fdb0720" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158002/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d5702360-c7bf-55fb-bf9c-3597406e0e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158002/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "37fa1935-2489-5a76-a52d-a57af05e1c69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158002/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "364d4895-7821-588d-8882-a142b42c777c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158002/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "d2e517d8-1f68-5d43-83d2-6e039e6d0634" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158002/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "9feb2e74-f747-57d4-8b97-8116d0ee0c75" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158002/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "1a055fd9-0617-50fb-a775-e3d958e8e16c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158002/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "0974579d-ff02-5b3e-ba9b-31d6d8583f06" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158002/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "371c5200-94ba-5835-973b-4d663d34437a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158002/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-158002/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-158002/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-158002/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-158002/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-158002/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-158002/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-158002/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-158002/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158002" :question/id #uuid "c784e4b5-c0e3-5a41-9985-7a5efc723545" :question/math-academy-id "q-158002" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic equation $2{x}^{2}+x-4=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - The discriminant of the equation is a perfect square.\nII. - The equation has only rational solutions.\nIII. - The equation has only irrational solutions." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have $a=2,$ $b=1,$ and $c=-4.$ So, we calculate the discriminant as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & =(1)^{2}-4(2)(-4) \\\\  & =1+32 \\\\  & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd $33$ is *not* a perfect square.\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true.\n\nFirst, notice that our quadratic equation has rational coefficients. And, since the discriminant is not a perfect square, the equation must have two irrational solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-158002/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "adc75098-5640-5e81-a0bc-003fa20c090c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158002"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84333/selection/f37f939de3c7c1325a0f6228d6e99fe0f6658cb541ff37fd6846a6cdf8e9df4f" :answer/id #uuid "9b232213-17cc-5460-8d11-a63369663d07" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Yes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84333/selection/34979fb822d3590f46e11eb2ad63f3336b59fc2faf7dca280a8f403745fcfdb9" :answer/id #uuid "70b0e3a8-4d90-5091-bb3a-1b048582423e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84333/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "51cfe37c-18ab-5778-81da-b1dc936be0f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84333/selection/f37f939de3c7c1325a0f6228d6e99fe0f6658cb541ff37fd6846a6cdf8e9df4f" :answer-field/choices ["q-84333/selection/f37f939de3c7c1325a0f6228d6e99fe0f6658cb541ff37fd6846a6cdf8e9df4f" "q-84333/selection/34979fb822d3590f46e11eb2ad63f3336b59fc2faf7dca280a8f403745fcfdb9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84333" :question/id #uuid "ba0cd7e7-1913-5003-b315-15357e8d1f1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-84333" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/5b3030b99501d2f3bc7dec80c4a1eab3754096c633be6d6d309064b084a8351d.png)\n\nIs the Venn diagram above correct?" :question/worked-solution "For any event $X,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(X)+P({X}^{'})=1.\n$$\n\nThe Venn diagram tells us that $P(X)=\\frac{5}{8}$ and $P({X}^{'})=\\frac{3}{8}.$\n\nThese probabilities satisfy the rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X)+P({X}^{'}) & =\\frac{5}{8}+\\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the above Venn diagram is  correct." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84333/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450401ad-3c58-5c15-ab78-b5e1ccf42a85"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84333"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119376/answer/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "bb8457db-f6e5-5ddd-b57d-62da772ce615" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119376/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a980036-158c-5b0c-a902-64f2cba3f24e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-119376/answer/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-119376/answer/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119376" :question/id #uuid "d531bcc0-5aad-57d1-a7e6-bdcbfb0a5d04" :question/math-academy-id "q-119376" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/ff6cdd3a9cc650842bba6e546cc91fca3206279cb6d8f9d835357c3cdcb597ce.png)\n\nConsider the sample space $S$ with the Venn diagram given above. What is the value of a constant $b?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "From the given Venn diagram, we have $P(X)=\\frac{1}{b}$ and $P({X}^{'})=\\frac{2}{b}.$\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X)+P({X}^{'}) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{b}+\\frac{2}{b} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{b} & =1 \\\\ b & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119376/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450401ad-3c58-5c15-ab78-b5e1ccf42a85"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119376"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84428/answer/cb69a2cee94d066e797c8817f9478c282b4df4f9410863e07a754e6c3274ab5c" :answer/id #uuid "1e1fbceb-950d-5d19-b414-6ec16db91287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84428/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "2110b3f7-3f9a-50ba-ba22-2e0a49a6d572" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-84428/answer/cb69a2cee94d066e797c8817f9478c282b4df4f9410863e07a754e6c3274ab5c" :answer-field/choices ["q-84428/answer/cb69a2cee94d066e797c8817f9478c282b4df4f9410863e07a754e6c3274ab5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84428" :question/id #uuid "e42f1d76-ec91-5e77-92f4-de1b8c4d9852" :question/math-academy-id "q-84428" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/f4928f6453f0f4d2e26dd99753e690de0b0266f63b541bf849c8fde5c13593d1.png)\n\nGiven the above sample space, find $P({X}^{'}).$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The Venn diagram tells us that $P(X)=\\frac{7}{13}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({X}^{'}) & =1-P(X) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{7}{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84428/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbb5348e-e292-513f-8b0a-90428692fc0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84428"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11590/answer/be2996522c88880b85c94a2df96123acadb7ac9f8da34e41793102bb8efe9a83" :answer/id #uuid "94828c53-dd84-5288-9dd4-b29c5a5e99d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.075" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11590/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1cb15b4-dbff-5269-a982-d08e38e581a4" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-11590/answer/be2996522c88880b85c94a2df96123acadb7ac9f8da34e41793102bb8efe9a83" :answer-field/choices ["q-11590/answer/be2996522c88880b85c94a2df96123acadb7ac9f8da34e41793102bb8efe9a83"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11590" :question/id #uuid "18160ae9-a2e7-570f-b9a7-71d46ee99dc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-11590" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/d773ba5052937e20997d5039fe4de6958862c4553cbe0edd8fdfe12eeb5de8fa.png)\n\nGiven the above sample space, find $P({X}^{'}).$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The Venn diagram tells us that $P(X)=0.925.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({X}^{'}) & =1-P(X) \\\\  & =1-0.925 \\\\  & =0.075.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11590/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbb5348e-e292-513f-8b0a-90428692fc0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11590"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119406/answer/0d87e7aed5b7af234c0763c1f6bdf2976ee93b9b4dbb60d5c11df0bc346f1e27" :answer/id #uuid "695bb784-c889-5b24-b8b4-10b5a10508ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8766" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119406/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a4b6805-4f60-5a64-b64d-a1da46c28340" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-119406/answer/0d87e7aed5b7af234c0763c1f6bdf2976ee93b9b4dbb60d5c11df0bc346f1e27" :answer-field/choices ["q-119406/answer/0d87e7aed5b7af234c0763c1f6bdf2976ee93b9b4dbb60d5c11df0bc346f1e27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119406" :question/id #uuid "63041fbf-1c6b-5528-a9b1-540c3e1c23bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-119406" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/c700c7a205ab674275e2e9f0b2dd79054853dfeaf33f6794d6d7e4196389274b.png)\n\nGiven the above sample space, find $P(X).$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The Venn diagram tells us that $P({X}^{'})=0.1234.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X) & =1-P({X}^{'}) \\\\  & =1-0.1234 \\\\  & =0.8766.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-119406/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af4cfa4a-7f49-50c9-a875-ce51c3874c4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119406"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42070/answer/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "924ec03f-ea5a-5596-8164-807f45e54f59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42070/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1e24f39-9ec8-541f-9dc3-1a38b67d0f37" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-42070/answer/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer-field/choices ["q-42070/answer/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42070" :question/id #uuid "60abed17-1948-5b76-9695-4adb8b2b042e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42070" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/4decd7da6d460540762f6cb2c32fcd36bc7f3c9e24fb62af9244afe0c29dbba4.png)\n\nConsider the sample space $S$ with the Venn diagram given above. What is $P(A)?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "From the given Venn diagram, we have $P(A)=y$ and $P({A}^{'})=\\frac{y}{5}.$\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A)+P({A}^{'}) & =1 \\\\ y+\\frac{y}{5} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{6y}{5} & =1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,  $P(A)=y=\\frac{5}{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42070/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af4cfa4a-7f49-50c9-a875-ce51c3874c4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42070"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-67439/answer/ecbf644e0f3159399d70e723c861c693203df3e95bd582ad9c72fde6bbe8157c" :answer/id #uuid "34c48104-4fe1-5365-a916-797f9ea4ad0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67439/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "bace9fc5-2f38-5ab3-b01e-2f59a7d5e614" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-67439/answer/ecbf644e0f3159399d70e723c861c693203df3e95bd582ad9c72fde6bbe8157c" :answer-field/choices ["q-67439/answer/ecbf644e0f3159399d70e723c861c693203df3e95bd582ad9c72fde6bbe8157c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-67439" :question/id #uuid "d177fcdc-42ce-5f5f-82c6-0abf2f8ef727" :question/math-academy-id "q-67439" :question/problem "Solve the equation $-\\frac{2}{x+3}=\\frac{8}{x-1}.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that\n\n- $x=-3$ cannot be a solution since this would make the denominator on the left-hand side zero\n\n- $x=1$ cannot be a solution since this would make the denominator on the right-hand side zero\n\nWe can flip an equation involving two fractions as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{c}{d}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{d}{c}\n$$\n\nThe above technique works whenever $a$ and $c$ are both different from zero.\n\nTherefore, we can flip the given equation as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{x+3}{2}=\\frac{x-1}{8}\n$$\n\nNext, we write both fractions using the least common denominator, $8.$ The equation becomes\n\n$$\n-\\frac{4x+12}{8}=\\frac{x-1}{8}.\n$$\n\nWe can now solve this equation with the addition and the multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)\\cdot \\frac{4x+12}{-8} & =(-8)\\cdot \\frac{x-1}{8} \\\\ 4x+12 & =-x+1 \\\\ 4x+x & =1-12 \\\\ 5x & =-11 \\\\ (\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (5x) & =(\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (-11) \\\\ (\\cancel{\\frac{1}{5}})\\cdot (\\cancel{5}x) & =(\\frac{1}{5})\\cdot (-11) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{11}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-67439/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "387a794f-17ea-5ea9-86a1-656a495f62cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-67439"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-27119/fixed-cost-dollars/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "9d5f00b7-431a-52b8-bd0e-de7f2d0920d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-27119/fixed-cost-dollars" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5e10668-a6d6-5975-8c55-97b66a157a63" :answer-field/key "fixed-cost-dollars" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-27119/fixed-cost-dollars/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-27119/fixed-cost-dollars/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-27119/hourly-cost-dollars/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "06618f90-a631-555c-abb4-a72f42d27da2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-27119/hourly-cost-dollars" :answer-field/id #uuid "8669d754-973c-5e79-9ec8-918a525175c2" :answer-field/key "hourly-cost-dollars" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-27119/hourly-cost-dollars/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-27119/hourly-cost-dollars/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-27119" :question/id #uuid "e04818ed-156e-5291-ac08-af963c259b25" :question/math-academy-id "q-27119" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/01509c920e5b7578569ca48b0dac5e3688e17818f02614627d907349ef8887b3.png)\n\nThe graph above represents the hourly cost of a boat ride at a certain lake. What is the actual cost of a boat ride?\n\nFixed cost dollars: {{fixed-cost-dollars}}\n\nHourly cost dollars: {{hourly-cost-dollars}}" :question/worked-solution "The graph has a $y$-intercept at $(0,20),$ which means that the cost is $$20$ even when no time has been elapsed. So, the boat rental charges an initial fee of $$20.00.$\n\nTo find the cost per hour, notice that the units of the slope are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{dollars}}{\\text{hours}},\n$$\n\nor dollars per hour. So, to calculate the cost per hour, we need to calculate the slope of the line. \n\nSince the line passes through the points $(0,20)$ and $(4,40)$, we find its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40-20}{4-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{4} \\\\  & =5\\text{ dollars/hour}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cost of a ride is $$20.00$ plus $$5.00$ per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-27119/fixed-cost-dollars" "q-27119/hourly-cost-dollars"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e55d466-a5c0-5b55-b26d-67e1e1994f20"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-27119"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251801/answer/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "24962c24-9463-5871-a0e7-ab0af6b4c469" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251801/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "122b14cc-b665-5bdd-8b84-5beae7306db6" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251801/answer/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-251801/answer/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251801" :question/id #uuid "aaa5a8d3-ddc5-5495-addf-51ebb0019cf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-251801" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $1$ | $7$ | $3$ | $4$ | $6$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $11$ | $3$ | $7$ | $2$ | $1$ | $18$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=247,$ calculate ${S}_{xy}.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of products of deviations from the means can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} & =1+7+3+4+6+10=31, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} & =11+3+7+2+1+18=42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=247.$\n\nFinally, by substituting in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xy}=247-\\frac{1}{6}(31)(42)=247-217=30.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-251801/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251801"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113479/answer/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "3a8760a4-fc31-5c9a-9404-6afacf46f9b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113479/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfc220ac-902f-57ac-b892-b71e8daa3106" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-113479/answer/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-113479/answer/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113479" :question/id #uuid "fa5f1c4b-9c02-56f6-92b6-f8a6f5b1eec5" :question/math-academy-id "q-113479" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/65348161e386fac14a98e8440d32d3883b5865a6d1eecfcd58e12931730ad0b8.png)\n\nThe graph represents the function $y=\\frac{a}{x-b}+k.$ What is the value of $a+b+k?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the horizontal asymptote of the graph is $y=2,$ while the vertical asymptote is $x=1.$ This means that $k=2$ and $b=1,$ and we can re-write our function as\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{a}{x-1}+2.\n$$\n\nAlso, we are given that the point $(2,5)$ lies on the graph. Substituting its coordinates into the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{a}{x-1}+2 \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{a}{2-1}+2 \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{a}{1} \\\\ a & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+k=3+1+2=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-113479/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "308f3685-0a90-56f3-9653-a83cec4286d2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113479"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-51567/answer/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "437dcd9d-2381-5665-8812-6db4db373dcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51567/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b6689cc-424a-5a03-b855-95578f1e475f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-51567/answer/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-51567/answer/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51567" :question/id #uuid "d428032a-dc8a-5dbd-8dd9-59088ffcca86" :question/math-academy-id "q-51567" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/4585ab21f7130a45e2ff5871e0fdc66cda5483181033010519781d9725eec36a.png)\n\nThe graph of a periodic function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. What is the period of this function?\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that if we shift the graph $3$ units left or right, the graph remains unchanged.\n\nOn the other hand, if we shift the graph horizontally by any distance other than $3$ (or a multiple of $3$), we get a different graph.\n\nTherefore, the period of the function is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-51567/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ebe5738-7682-55ad-a21b-235063f08b88"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51567"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78174/answer/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "01a9ebd0-86ba-5c34-a369-64423eeab091" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78174/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "35071f1f-348f-5c85-b1cf-cbec76d25c45" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-78174/answer/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer-field/choices ["q-78174/answer/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78174" :question/id #uuid "e900665d-2790-5224-833b-dae8d3b97390" :question/math-academy-id "q-78174" :question/problem "Given that  $(3{w}^{2}+w+5)({w}^{2}+w+1)=3{w}^{4}+a{w}^{3}+b{w}^{2}+cw+5,$ calculate $a+b+c.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "We distribute all three terms of the trinomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3{w}^{2}+w+5)({w}^{2}+w+1) & = \\\\ 3{w}^{2}({w}^{2}+w+1)+w({w}^{2}+w+1)+5({w}^{2}+w+1) & = \\\\ 3{w}^{4}+3{w}^{3}+3{w}^{2}+{w}^{3}+{w}^{2}+w+5{w}^{2}+5w+5 & = \\\\ 3{w}^{4}+4{w}^{3}+9{w}^{2}+6w+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=4,$ $b=9,$ and $c=6.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b+c=4+9+6=19.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78174/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7019d52-33a1-5968-9a93-2f2f06fbb0d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78174"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111362/answer/2341d4beafc19cb7b8396e0b9f21c544ec7f6a786fc846e9361e36afd0b43437" :answer/id #uuid "9c396da7-833f-5cec-855b-b86b88810cce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "43" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111362/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "668faa38-775f-5725-a250-436066030f64" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-111362/answer/2341d4beafc19cb7b8396e0b9f21c544ec7f6a786fc846e9361e36afd0b43437" :answer-field/choices ["q-111362/answer/2341d4beafc19cb7b8396e0b9f21c544ec7f6a786fc846e9361e36afd0b43437"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111362" :question/id #uuid "55058b06-dd5d-5caa-a687-35d85c6cc189" :question/math-academy-id "q-111362" :question/problem "Given that  $(3{s}^{2}+2s+4)({s}^{2}+3s+2)=3{s}^{4}+a{s}^{3}+b{s}^{2}+cs+8,$ calculate $a+b+c.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "We distribute all three terms of the trinomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3{s}^{2}+2s+4)({s}^{2}+3s+2) & = \\\\ 3{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+3s+2)+(2s)({s}^{2}+3s+2)+(4)({s}^{2}+3s+2) & = \\\\ 3{s}^{4}+9{s}^{3}+6{s}^{2}+2{s}^{3}+6{s}^{2}+4s+4{s}^{2}+12s+8 & = \\\\ 3{s}^{4}+11{s}^{3}+16{s}^{2}+16s+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=11,$ $b=16,$ and $c=16.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b+c=11+16+16=43.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-111362/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7019d52-33a1-5968-9a93-2f2f06fbb0d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111362"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2744/answer/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3e6b6660-132b-5586-919d-7c2c56fcd3d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2744/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "629df364-ddee-5d51-82ac-3a4435a44823" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-2744/answer/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-2744/answer/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2744" :question/id #uuid "1fa68d8e-2ff3-5778-8627-de03a66add46" :question/math-academy-id "q-2744" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of $ac$ in the product $(a+b+c)(a-b-c)?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "We distribute the terms of the trinomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+b+c)(a-b-c) & = \\\\ a(a-b-c)+b(a-b-c)+c(a-b-c) & = \\\\ {a}^{2}-ab-ac+ba-{b}^{2}-bc+ca-cb-{c}^{2} & = \\\\ {a}^{2}-{b}^{2}+0ab+0ac-2bc-{c}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the coefficient of $ac$ is $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-2744/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09357892-5d4b-5346-99b0-9babc7b0d574"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2744"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31383/answer/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "66d3f27d-31a7-5ebb-a2b6-ef885bbff640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31383/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3ac9484-9a16-54ca-ad81-23e24fe0f882" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-31383/answer/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-31383/answer/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31383" :question/id #uuid "cf4dcdbc-9168-55c3-a5fe-dc072fb8a7ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-31383" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of ${x}^{2}y$ in the product $(2x+y)({x}^{2}-2xy+3{y}^{2})?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "We distribute both terms of the binomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x+y)({x}^{2}-2xy+3{y}^{2}) & = \\\\ 2x({x}^{2}-2xy+3{y}^{2})+y({x}^{2}-2xy+3{y}^{2}) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}y+6x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y-2x{y}^{2}+3{y}^{3} & = \\\\ 2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+4x{y}^{2}+3{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{2}y$ is $-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31383/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09357892-5d4b-5346-99b0-9babc7b0d574"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31383"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86424/answer/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "8683c5c9-de60-5c5a-b120-a61da703cf14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86424/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "4abfcb06-3ae1-5b51-bf96-dd3c3c9a2972" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-86424/answer/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer-field/choices ["q-86424/answer/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86424" :question/id #uuid "2b2a5aa3-5b37-5fc1-a953-21f39ffa3a31" :question/math-academy-id "q-86424" :question/problem "Given an arithmetic sequence that has $f(2)=5$ and $f(4)=23$, what is the index of the term $158?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "To construct the formula for the sequence, we need to know the common difference $d$ and the first term $f(1).$\n\nSince we are given $f(2)=5$ and $f(4)=23,$ we can find the common difference by dividing the total difference by the number of jumps:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{f(4)-f(2)}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{23-5}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{2} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(2)=5$ is $1$ jump after $f(1),$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =f(1)+d \\\\ 5 & =f(1)+9 \\\\ -4 & =f(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-4+(n-1)(9) \\\\  & =-4+9n-9 \\\\  & =9n-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives $f(n)=158,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =9n-13 \\\\ 158 & =9n-13 \\\\ 171 & =9n \\\\ \\frac{171}{9} & =n \\\\ 19 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $158$ is the $19$th term of the sequence." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86424/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d979a7bd-42a1-5d4f-8717-1caa06ce623c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86424"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108753/answer/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "e7ca1c0e-9830-57d1-87c2-d2f47a0da86d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108753/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "58811d5d-80b6-5d2c-a9b9-9f2b21d3a4c5" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-108753/answer/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer-field/choices ["q-108753/answer/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108753" :question/id #uuid "97acde06-7ca9-5d94-b594-1bd2bd789eb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-108753" :question/problem "What is the index of the term $104$ in the following arithmetic sequence?\n\n$$\n4,\\,9,\\,14,\\,…\n$$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Since ${a}_{1}=4$ and \n\n$$\nd=9-4=5,\n$$\n\nwe can construct the formula for the $n$th term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =4+(n-1)(5) \\\\  & =4+5n-5 \\\\  & =5n-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=104,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =5n-1 \\\\ 104 & =5n-1 \\\\ 105 & =5n \\\\ 21 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $105$ is the $21$st term of the sequence." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-108753/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d905f41-5940-547e-b3d2-558c6b881b68"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108753"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-236405/field-1/30d87289ce9cf4ee21b8a2dd0c77a8f827960a63af81df54e0fe73dfc1b823fc" :answer/id #uuid "9c1e0907-cbdd-53ab-aaa6-0ae6df7e2e58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "47" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236405/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "56f11ef7-23d3-513f-bdba-0ada206ca470" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-236405/field-1/30d87289ce9cf4ee21b8a2dd0c77a8f827960a63af81df54e0fe73dfc1b823fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-236405/field-1/30d87289ce9cf4ee21b8a2dd0c77a8f827960a63af81df54e0fe73dfc1b823fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-236405" :question/id #uuid "da63c57f-defb-510a-99d1-648360e671da" :question/math-academy-id "q-236405" :question/problem "In the arithmetic sequence $10,\\,6,\\,2,\\,…,$  the index of the term $-174$ is\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since ${a}_{1}=10$ and \n\n$$\nd=6-10=-4,\n$$\n\nwe can construct the formula for the $n$th term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =10+(n-1)(-4) \\\\  & =10-4n+4 \\\\  & =14-4n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=-174,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =14-4n \\\\ -174 & =14-4n \\\\ 4n & =188 \\\\ n & =47\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-174$ is the $47$th term of the sequence." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-236405/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d905f41-5940-547e-b3d2-558c6b881b68"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-236405"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-236651/field-1/87f70942b9483cb5cedbd7b4150ebc995451772f024ba0c75aaaea5741b3bd06" :answer/id #uuid "cdf94fc4-6c9c-59f7-ba15-07839a428f15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "68" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236651/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "66683034-f4a7-547a-b20c-9ccd03c1cb39" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-236651/field-1/87f70942b9483cb5cedbd7b4150ebc995451772f024ba0c75aaaea5741b3bd06" :answer-field/choices ["q-236651/field-1/87f70942b9483cb5cedbd7b4150ebc995451772f024ba0c75aaaea5741b3bd06"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-236651" :question/id #uuid "be5a0273-68d6-5b67-97bc-7c0cfdf78903" :question/math-academy-id "q-236651" :question/problem "In the arithmetic sequence $25,\\,16,\\,7,\\,…,$ the index of the term $-578$ is\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since ${a}_{1}=25$ and \n\n$$\nd=16-25=-9,\n$$\n\nwe can construct the formula for the $n$th term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =25+(n-1)(-9) \\\\  & =25-9n+9 \\\\  & =34-9n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=-578,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =34-9n \\\\ -578 & =34-9n \\\\ 9n & =612 \\\\ n & =68\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-578$ is the $68$th term of the sequence." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-236651/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d905f41-5940-547e-b3d2-558c6b881b68"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-236651"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-236849/field-1/4b741b651b6f24cd7370ee85fd4c2dd5b1d9bdb7c612965a77adc26bd59b4a9a" :answer/id #uuid "d90e1b69-99eb-55c2-8ac2-161678af393d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "41" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236849/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "38e8e6b5-a904-54c2-a46e-19858084a014" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-236849/field-1/4b741b651b6f24cd7370ee85fd4c2dd5b1d9bdb7c612965a77adc26bd59b4a9a" :answer-field/choices ["q-236849/field-1/4b741b651b6f24cd7370ee85fd4c2dd5b1d9bdb7c612965a77adc26bd59b4a9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-236849" :question/id #uuid "fde5764e-8989-5cce-8798-9652f3663ed9" :question/math-academy-id "q-236849" :question/problem "If an arithmetic sequence has ${a}_{3}=11$ and ${a}_{7}=15$, find the value of $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=49.$\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To construct the formula for the sequence, we need to know the common difference $d$ and the first term ${a}_{1}.$\n\nSince we are given ${a}_{3}=11$ and ${a}_{7}=15,$ we can find the common difference by dividing the total difference by the number of jumps:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{7}-{a}_{3}}{7-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{15-11}{7-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${a}_{3}=11$ is $2$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={a}_{1}+2d \\\\ 11 & ={a}_{1}+2(1) \\\\ 11 & ={a}_{1}+2 \\\\ 9 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =9+(n-1)(1) \\\\  & =9+n-1 \\\\  & =n+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=49,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =n+8 \\\\ 49 & =n+8 \\\\ 41 & =n \\\\ n & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $49$ is the $41$st term of the sequence." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-236849/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d979a7bd-42a1-5d4f-8717-1caa06ce623c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-236849"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123603/answer/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "8eba4139-203a-5d17-a0eb-a9b639997163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123603/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "30367d4b-ce68-51b4-8e84-d7dec3c0b71e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-123603/answer/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-123603/answer/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123603" :question/id #uuid "9e5a328a-ca83-5e2b-b8cf-4756149978bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-123603" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's remind ourselves of the special trigonometric ratios, as given by the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ corresponds to the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nSince the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123603/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0052499-42ab-5818-a844-20eb099c3f7b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123603"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123609/answer/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "54103ca5-dd3b-5843-bbe3-3e5f4f7ec8b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123609/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e5ab50b-a0de-5195-9cf0-1d6ce039d8ad" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-123609/answer/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-123609/answer/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123609" :question/id #uuid "13f67cae-eaf5-50b8-90bd-8b055038e1a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123609" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sec}{240}^{∘}=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's remind ourselves of the special trigonometric ratios, as given by the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle ${240}^{∘}$ corresponds to the point $(-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}).$\n\nSince the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{cos}{240}^{∘}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, using the fact that $\\operatorname{sec}\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}{240}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}{240}^{∘}}=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123609/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecd367ac-2a68-56d0-b553-85277a9c921d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123609"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-167226/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "ad23ad81-a361-5276-9f48-f95626f61826" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167226/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1dbe85ba-bf16-554c-8d3e-5e4bd5bc731b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-167226/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-167226/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-167226/field-2/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer/id #uuid "a98733b2-2845-5316-abd1-cf18d0dca11a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167226/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "54828145-6d13-5a11-a9c1-05c77a89323a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-167226/field-2/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer-field/choices ["q-167226/field-2/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-167226" :question/id #uuid "8d63494e-5f74-557b-a601-72890b90758c" :question/math-academy-id "q-167226" :question/problem "The coefficients $a$ and $b$ also satisfy the equation $70a+9b=600.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$b\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}b=75-5a \\\\ 70a+9b=600\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=75-5a\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $b$ in the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70a+9b & =600 \\\\ 70a+9(75-5a) & =600 \\\\ 70a+675-45a & =600 \\\\ 25a+675 & =600 \\\\ 25a & =-75 \\\\ a & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-3$ into $b=75-5a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =75-5(-3) \\\\ b & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-3,\\,b=90.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-167226/field-1" "q-167226/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-167226"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-167227/field-1/10574cfb2c5c143de701c99e35934484981801b5e0f43b46790744aa6a3c3bef" :answer/id #uuid "051bf4e8-235e-5157-adbf-b32ce8b74141" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "375" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167227/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "74514ad4-4047-575e-b3bc-9e156f7147ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-167227/field-1/10574cfb2c5c143de701c99e35934484981801b5e0f43b46790744aa6a3c3bef" :answer-field/choices ["q-167227/field-1/10574cfb2c5c143de701c99e35934484981801b5e0f43b46790744aa6a3c3bef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-167227" :question/id #uuid "6efda865-3762-5c97-a1e1-be30152c52c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-167227" :question/problem "Determine the daily profit if the company produces $25$ luxury white chocolate boxes in a day.\n\nThe company will earn$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$dollars." :question/worked-solution "From part 3, we have the function $p(x)=-3{x}^{2}+90x.$\n\nWe substitute $x=25$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(25) & =-3(25)^{2}+90(25) \\\\  & =-1\\,875+2\\,250 \\\\  & =375\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the company will earn $$375.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-167227/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e5366dd-a374-5abd-bdf6-77f378f97145"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-167227"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-167229/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "eb1ba20d-813b-5415-993b-3a79e31ed28e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-167229/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b3cb1c6-fc04-50f8-86d3-976bbe0f949b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-167229/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-167229/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-167229" :question/id #uuid "dcb05104-1d9d-5307-88a8-33037d9f7de1" :question/math-academy-id "q-167229" :question/problem "Find the minimum number of luxury white chocolate boxes the company needs to produce per day to make a daily profit of $$600.$\n\nThe company needs to produce$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ luxury white chocolate boxes per day." :question/worked-solution "From part 5, the required number of white chocolate boxes $x$ is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\n3\\cdot ({x}^{2}-30x+200)=0.\n$$\n\nDividing this equation by $3,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-30x+200=0.\n$$\n\nTo solve this equation, we want to find a factor pair of the constant term $(200)$ that also adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-30).$ The required factors are $(-10)$ and $(-20).$\n\nUsing this factor pair, we write the linear term as $-30x=-10x-20x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-30x+200 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-10x-20x+200 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-10x-20x+200 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-10x)+(-20x+200) & =0 \\\\ x(x-10)-20(x-10) & =0 \\\\ (x-10)(x-20)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the solutions are $x=10$ or $x=20.$ Since we require the minimum solution, we conclude that the company needs to produce $10$ luxury white chocolate boxes per day to make a profit of $$600.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-167229/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c9ba00d-9171-5732-8539-2e2943cce58e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-167229"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124419/selection/550a4db61128d9c1beff3d01835669e791feb0475caedef29e5aadd31fef7b69" :answer/id #uuid "f9b02ae1-79a5-5d4c-a37c-8d33b7bd5b37" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124419/selection/06281aae74d7faea230651a1647185a4d75cfb9af4f09878757300d90ede7a44" :answer/id #uuid "b52fd012-8d14-5245-b910-5611e50ab1e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124419/selection/5e4e50d8679ab7cbb399672d5dfa58626ba26e07675e3874f33209f062fa09e2" :answer/id #uuid "8d03dfd0-283c-508e-808d-7b02fc18538d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124419/selection/ee97e5e14bc1feff0a3e45a9d3431716386c64a369a01f1d18dba83235d227b4" :answer/id #uuid "f5a96c4f-bcd1-5e88-8d4a-f9e0848917fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant IV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124419/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cda67690-29b3-505f-9114-ae1f87b12f1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124419/selection/5e4e50d8679ab7cbb399672d5dfa58626ba26e07675e3874f33209f062fa09e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-124419/selection/550a4db61128d9c1beff3d01835669e791feb0475caedef29e5aadd31fef7b69" "q-124419/selection/06281aae74d7faea230651a1647185a4d75cfb9af4f09878757300d90ede7a44" "q-124419/selection/5e4e50d8679ab7cbb399672d5dfa58626ba26e07675e3874f33209f062fa09e2" "q-124419/selection/ee97e5e14bc1feff0a3e45a9d3431716386c64a369a01f1d18dba83235d227b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124419" :question/id #uuid "b02b1783-580f-5ba0-8828-54461d71b13a" :question/math-academy-id "q-124419" :question/problem "The angle $\\theta ={940}^{∘}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with ${940}^{∘}$ by *subtracting* integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$\n\n- ${940}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}={580}^{∘}$\n\n- ${940}^{∘}-2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={220}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle ${220}^{∘}$ is coterminal with ${940}^{∘}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/fda42bbc304e20454045766c7e6dffeeb4ecc65da14b6e89dd75f0a4be788afa.png)\n\nWe see that ${220}^{∘}$ lies in quadrant III. Therefore, ${940}^{∘}$ also lies in this quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124419/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a119150-6d23-59bd-90c9-699de3a75795"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124419"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64684/selection/550a4db61128d9c1beff3d01835669e791feb0475caedef29e5aadd31fef7b69" :answer/id #uuid "712753df-61f6-5b8d-aac1-8334199f6c95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64684/selection/06281aae74d7faea230651a1647185a4d75cfb9af4f09878757300d90ede7a44" :answer/id #uuid "8a098b45-c2e8-5184-ad1b-26d16ee81d23" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64684/selection/5e4e50d8679ab7cbb399672d5dfa58626ba26e07675e3874f33209f062fa09e2" :answer/id #uuid "f1ce7416-c18b-595c-8946-699ee597f39c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64684/selection/ee97e5e14bc1feff0a3e45a9d3431716386c64a369a01f1d18dba83235d227b4" :answer/id #uuid "43d72985-f62c-5dcf-b5d5-ca0c6215fc29" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant IV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64684/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3612bfb5-d8b9-5b06-9025-f70807e1466e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64684/selection/06281aae74d7faea230651a1647185a4d75cfb9af4f09878757300d90ede7a44" :answer-field/choices ["q-64684/selection/550a4db61128d9c1beff3d01835669e791feb0475caedef29e5aadd31fef7b69" "q-64684/selection/06281aae74d7faea230651a1647185a4d75cfb9af4f09878757300d90ede7a44" "q-64684/selection/5e4e50d8679ab7cbb399672d5dfa58626ba26e07675e3874f33209f062fa09e2" "q-64684/selection/ee97e5e14bc1feff0a3e45a9d3431716386c64a369a01f1d18dba83235d227b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64684" :question/id #uuid "45b2051b-479f-542d-97fb-8807ff31a294" :question/math-academy-id "q-64684" :question/problem "The angle $\\theta =\\frac{17\\pi }{6}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{17\\pi }{6}$ by *subtracting* integer multiples of $2\\pi $ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n- $\\frac{17\\pi }{6}-2\\pi =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle $\\frac{17\\pi }{6}$ is coterminal with $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/1c7c1d3a8d69502521dc71f24335ff79e707867161b95d6a80eaf95c0bf6e36c.png)\n\nWe see that $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ lies in quadrant II. Therefore, $\\frac{17\\pi }{6}$ also lies in this quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64684/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a119150-6d23-59bd-90c9-699de3a75795"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64684"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124719/selection/550a4db61128d9c1beff3d01835669e791feb0475caedef29e5aadd31fef7b69" :answer/id #uuid "e0afcaf6-96f9-5f04-b47a-1f7fc76fdae6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124719/selection/06281aae74d7faea230651a1647185a4d75cfb9af4f09878757300d90ede7a44" :answer/id #uuid "997613b3-bfc8-5ed3-ba9e-bfe36a2278ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124719/selection/5e4e50d8679ab7cbb399672d5dfa58626ba26e07675e