)\n\nWe see that $\\frac{13\\pi }{10}$ lies in quadrant III. Therefore, $-\\frac{27\\pi }{10}$ also lies in this quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124719/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "993c8fe4-dae9-5dc4-9f94-5012f905e0ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124719"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64678/selection/550a4db61128d9c1beff3d01835669e791feb0475caedef29e5aadd31fef7b69" :answer/id #uuid "74a27f2d-4de7-5c12-bf80-2bc0547ebf19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64678/selection/06281aae74d7faea230651a1647185a4d75cfb9af4f09878757300d90ede7a44" :answer/id #uuid "40cfb998-cdc7-5a8a-9862-40b40601bcad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant II" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64678/selection/5e4e50d8679ab7cbb399672d5dfa58626ba26e07675e3874f33209f062fa09e2" :answer/id #uuid "949b5bce-4f4d-5782-b3a1-58fb0babf6a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64678/selection/ee97e5e14bc1feff0a3e45a9d3431716386c64a369a01f1d18dba83235d227b4" :answer/id #uuid "73c35910-0338-58bf-9e5d-77001c9a61d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Quadrant IV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64678/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a2c4789-d7f3-566b-8e6b-156289316c1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64678/selection/550a4db61128d9c1beff3d01835669e791feb0475caedef29e5aadd31fef7b69" :answer-field/choices ["q-64678/selection/550a4db61128d9c1beff3d01835669e791feb0475caedef29e5aadd31fef7b69" "q-64678/selection/06281aae74d7faea230651a1647185a4d75cfb9af4f09878757300d90ede7a44" "q-64678/selection/5e4e50d8679ab7cbb399672d5dfa58626ba26e07675e3874f33209f062fa09e2" "q-64678/selection/ee97e5e14bc1feff0a3e45a9d3431716386c64a369a01f1d18dba83235d227b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64678" :question/id #uuid "0e21b7ac-5788-524c-8ceb-e2c5880c1015" :question/math-academy-id "q-64678" :question/problem "The angle $\\theta =-{650}^{∘}$ is represented in the coordinate plane in the usual way. In which quadrant does it lie?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-{650}^{∘}$ by *adding* integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $({0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}].$\n\n- $-{650}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}=-{290}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{650}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={70}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nSo the angle ${70}^{∘}$ is coterminal with $-{650}^{∘}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/8dff305410da2b49c69006fdb84b4de6b481ccf2a526f42b18d2eae538601bfb.png)\n\nWe see that ${70}^{∘}$ lies in quadrant I. Therefore, $-{650}^{∘}$ also lies in this quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64678/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "993c8fe4-dae9-5dc4-9f94-5012f905e0ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64678"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125138/r1c1/6bb6fe4cbf49be857221580cc496029e4813795bce6a4086557bb8bc8141d0b9" :answer/id #uuid "186922e0-79e7-5bea-a1c9-9dc53e50e9f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125138/r1c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a95cd3-7d33-5b9e-86f2-7f568b3a6e4e" :answer-field/key "r1c1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-125138/r1c1/6bb6fe4cbf49be857221580cc496029e4813795bce6a4086557bb8bc8141d0b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-125138/r1c1/6bb6fe4cbf49be857221580cc496029e4813795bce6a4086557bb8bc8141d0b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125138/r2c1/7ce48957c13cbafdbde3c59b7102237d54bec504ad28dcba8b06917cdb6cc51d" :answer/id #uuid "fc68583d-2af0-5183-94e7-b79dc5a4617b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125138/r2c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "05f5166b-2a10-5206-90d3-d3328b1a0f86" :answer-field/key "r2c1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-125138/r2c1/7ce48957c13cbafdbde3c59b7102237d54bec504ad28dcba8b06917cdb6cc51d" :answer-field/choices ["q-125138/r2c1/7ce48957c13cbafdbde3c59b7102237d54bec504ad28dcba8b06917cdb6cc51d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125138" :question/id #uuid "bde60051-298e-59aa-a76e-9c9fabb0aba6" :question/math-academy-id "q-125138" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction.\n\nRow 1, column 1: {{r1c1}}\n\nRow 2, column 1: {{r2c1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+b & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0+5 \\\\ 4+8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2a+b| & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(2a+b) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{13} \\\\ \\frac{12}{13}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-125138/r1c1" "q-125138/r2c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c45a70b-273c-5fec-a768-40a1cf218628"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102106/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "1a6b88e9-537f-5014-904c-2f3c5e74a690" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102106/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e969ed7d-a030-5bbe-b5ff-e06b6ecf3ffc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102106/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "0fe4a6d4-d9a3-509d-a10f-a48daed15eb4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102106/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "3d948c4c-a856-5a84-a62a-0e142b8c5423" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102106/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "a1943369-4326-5ce8-828f-6f497c0387c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102106/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "8803f1cd-97ad-5de2-a183-cf168dc86ebb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102106/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "ce416271-d959-5f29-a613-74527db0fb36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102106/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "8b0aa4ce-2595-57a5-9575-ac87a8f8dd0a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102106/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf8d454-a5e4-5c07-b361-eea7a481c457" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102106/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-102106/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-102106/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-102106/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-102106/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-102106/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-102106/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-102106/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-102106/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102106" :question/id #uuid "6b31ab2b-c4c5-5adb-93e3-725f33b127ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-102106" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/d9cf9a5c61cbf1796cf6682b129b4c05171c364c7b34e7cce176ba27e9c9cb24.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nI. - $x=-1$\nII. - $x=2$\nIII. - $x=4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=4.$ Since there is an asymptote at $x=4,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=4$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  \"I and II only\".\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/95967eb82512aae261936a6c09e2f474c72c9a130d3ecb527f62408822d88c96.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102106/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102106"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-1803/answer/de71689db3524c73722131e4d2c999a60a9161a4dc41cd04b5bc49a49e61f6ab" :answer/id #uuid "03404903-6661-5ae8-b691-ba3920cab111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "512" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1803/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "0196557c-c5ad-5730-928e-ed86abb7f003" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-1803/answer/de71689db3524c73722131e4d2c999a60a9161a4dc41cd04b5bc49a49e61f6ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-1803/answer/de71689db3524c73722131e4d2c999a60a9161a4dc41cd04b5bc49a49e61f6ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-1803" :question/id #uuid "9727e37f-7458-5fb2-9794-a48d52770acf" :question/math-academy-id "q-1803" :question/problem "A word consists of $3$ letters, as shown below:\n\n| Letter | Letter | Letter |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n\nHere, each \"Letter\" can be any capital from A-H ($8$ in total). How many possible words are there?\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "For each letter, there is a total of $8$ possibilities: A, B, C, D, E, F, G, and H.\n\nUsing the **rule of product**, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of words} & =\\text{Number of options in the first slot} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of options in the second slot} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of options in the third slot} \\\\  & =8\\times 8\\times 8 \\\\  & ={8}^{3} \\\\  & =512.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, there are $512$ possible words." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-1803/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f302298b-bae3-563f-9238-eb5f3280c556"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-1803"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-5759/answer/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer/id #uuid "917b7239-d1a9-58a5-ae89-76e89f4a79c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5759/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "31c1f32f-a92e-5062-8efa-0e6b7f45f5da" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-5759/answer/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer-field/choices ["q-5759/answer/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-5759" :question/id #uuid "749914bf-d1a3-5489-91da-4a74ce2608f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-5759" :question/problem "You're buying a new computer and can choose different options: $3$ different levels of RAM, $2$ different hard drive sizes, $3$ different monitor sizes, and $4$ different colors.  How many different computer systems can you create from these choices?\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the **rule of product**, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of computer systems} & =\\text{Number of RAM levels} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of hard drive sizes} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of monitor sizes} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of colors} \\\\  & =3\\times 2\\times 3\\times 4 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can create $72$ different computer systems." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-5759/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57bae420-d529-5b9d-a306-37127c523be6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5759"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-5760/answer/8248390a30a22ff62ef4244bbcb9b5331491b25abf17048d586db2d13b110445" :answer/id #uuid "dfad00bb-0495-5532-915c-4c3d81a054c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{5}^{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5760/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2b84597-acc5-5c3d-9c3c-d9cb9cddc42b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-5760/answer/8248390a30a22ff62ef4244bbcb9b5331491b25abf17048d586db2d13b110445" :answer-field/choices ["q-5760/answer/8248390a30a22ff62ef4244bbcb9b5331491b25abf17048d586db2d13b110445"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-5760" :question/id #uuid "98158fcc-db0f-530b-87f1-367cdd949729" :question/math-academy-id "q-5760" :question/problem "You're letting your computer make random songs using $5$ different notes, and you want the song to be $32$ notes long. All $32$ notes have the same duration. If notes can be repeated, how many different songs can your computer create?\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the **rule of product**, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of songs} & =\\text{Number of choices for the }1\\text{st note} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of choices for the }2\\text{nd note} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of choices for the }3\\text{rd note} \\\\  & \\times … \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of choices for the }32\\text{nd note} \\\\  & ={{5\\times 5\\times 5\\times ⋯\\times 5}_{⏟}}_{32\\text{ times}} \\\\  & ={5}^{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the computer can create ${5}^{32}$ different songs." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-5760/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57bae420-d529-5b9d-a306-37127c523be6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5760"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-92983/y/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "686dcbf3-9915-5d87-a73c-2fe61d91472e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92983/y" :answer-field/id #uuid "5bb8367a-3808-5ada-bad9-70a6c5853a45" :answer-field/key "y" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-92983/y/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-92983/y/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-92983" :question/id #uuid "6fe18260-df06-55c2-bd92-ef2821897be4" :question/math-academy-id "q-92983" :question/problem "Find the equation of the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)={3}^{x}-1.$\n\n$y =$: {{y}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/d03c7a1ada2f422df96b8479894197e5d388f73e1f7980155a009b6502902cbb.png)\n\nSince the function approaches the line $y=-1$ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we conclude that the equation of the horizontal asymptote is $y=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-92983/y"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c2518d5-0fde-5dfc-aa07-f1bdd3c1585a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-92983"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-92990/y/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "f22c16fc-f6c1-5051-834f-8ea7f4851607" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92990/y" :answer-field/id #uuid "692c0975-83dd-5e12-b8d5-3f74e2e8e1e1" :answer-field/key "y" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-92990/y/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-92990/y/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-92990" :question/id #uuid "8e2b0b19-242a-586c-83d9-b9a00d75b930" :question/math-academy-id "q-92990" :question/problem "Find the equation of the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}({2}^{2x+1})+3.$\n\n$y =$: {{y}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/7df3ad89847be8197653ece86935a3e310d66a7632143e5e5218bf489f1c23d4.png)\n\nSince the function approaches the line $y=3$ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we conclude that the equation of the horizontal asymptote is $y=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-92990/y"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c2518d5-0fde-5dfc-aa07-f1bdd3c1585a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-92990"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-47307/answer/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326" :answer/id #uuid "554267c3-b36b-53f1-96ea-a70a14233d73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47307/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1976e7b-5e56-5bf2-a749-123a4c7460f8" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-47307/answer/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326" :answer-field/choices ["q-47307/answer/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-47307" :question/id #uuid "3636bb28-36be-554b-b1a3-2ece301c26d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-47307" :question/problem "A group of randomly selected students from Chicago High School was asked which country they want to visit between Brazil, Spain, France, or Japan. The results of the survey are summarized in the two-way frequency table below.\n\n|  | Brazil | Spain | France | Japan | Totals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Girls | $12$ | $20$ | $9$ | $14$ | $55$ |\n| Boys | $14$ | $10$ | $20$ | $1$ | $45$ |\n| Totals | $26$ | $30$ | $29$ | $15$ | $100$ |\n\nBoston High School has $400$ students. Assuming that the distribution of the results is the same in both high schools, estimate the number of girls at Boston High School who wish to visit Brazil or France. Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "To estimate the number of girls who wish to visit Brazil or France, we\n\n- add up the numbers in the intersection of the row **\"Girls\"** and the column **\"Brazil\"** and the intersection of the row **\"Girls\"** and the column **\"France\"**, and then\n\n- divide by the total number of data points in the table.\n\n|  | Brazil | Spain | France | Japan | Totals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Girls | $12$ | $20$ | $9$ | $14$ | $55$ |\n| Boys | $14$ | $10$ | $20$ | $1$ | $45$ |\n| Totals | $26$ | $30$ | $29$ | $15$ | $100$ |\n\nAdding up these numbers and then dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(100),$ we get\n\n$$\np=\\frac{12+9}{100}=\\frac{21}{100}=0.21.\n$$\n\nThis represents the estimated probability that a randomly selected student is a girl who wishes to visit Brazil or France.\n\nFinally, to find the estimated number of girls of Boston High School who wish to visit Brazil or France, we multiply the total number of students in Boston High School $(400)$ by the probability above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =400\\cdot p \\\\  & =400\\cdot 0.21 \\\\  & =84\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-47307/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6956b58-5581-5221-8d4f-88ebde382f0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-47307"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-575/answer/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "841e8a1a-3c8b-5f97-965f-40251f13efe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-575/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "e656be50-0e8a-5b00-a570-bb0ae760e03d" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-575/answer/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-575/answer/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-575" :question/id #uuid "feb815e0-49a2-5a08-9510-a18cd36fc9e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-575" :question/problem "If $a={\\text{i}}^{2}$ then ${a}^{4}=$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the power law for exponents, we have\n\n$$\n{a}^{4}={({\\text{i}}^{2})}^{4}={\\text{i}}^{2\\cdot 4}={\\text{i}}^{8}.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\text{i}$ raised to some positive integer power $n$, we divide $n$ by $4,$ and raise $\\text{i}$ to the remainder.\n\nIn our case, we have $n=8.$ Dividing the power by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n8÷4=2\\,\\text{R}0.\n$$\n\nSo the remainder is $0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\text{i}}^{8}={\\text{i}}^{0}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-575/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35c51033-ad39-5776-9829-cf573214ef03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-575"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-66412/answer/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "7638ef27-f19f-5c5f-a5c1-11acc4e29d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66412/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "6821fbd9-b4f5-5206-b8ed-cd3fb89fc36b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-66412/answer/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-66412/answer/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-66412" :question/id #uuid "85eb992c-5f22-5219-9748-87d4d54a3ac2" :question/math-academy-id "q-66412" :question/problem "Given $f(x)={x}^{2}-6$ and $g(x)=-x+2,$ find  $(f-g)(4).$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The notation $(f-g)(x)$ means the difference of the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x).$ \n\n**Method 1** \n\nTo evaluate $(f-g)(4),$ we find $f(4)$ and $g(4),$ and then subtract $g(4)$ from $f(4).$\n\nSo, first we find $f(4)$ and $g(4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4) & =(4)^{2}-6=10 \\\\ g(4) & =-(4)+2=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we subtract $g(4)$ from $f(4)$:\n\n$$\n(f-g)(4)=f(4)-g(4)=10-(-2)=12\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst we find the difference of the two functions $f$ and $g$ by subtracting $g(x)$ from $f(x)$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f-g)(x) & =({x}^{2}-6)-(-x+2) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-6+x-2 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+x-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate $(f-g)(4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f-g)(4) & =(4)^{2}+4-8=12\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-66412/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e8b25b3-5cc4-51b7-8ff9-fc1773797ad4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98/answer/f8c741b26d6c252fd277bcaeae6e7c3326f626b9a3e0f43d8fd01cd3ffaa30e0" :answer/id #uuid "6310d092-8863-5a48-bb29-8e40b3e3e2f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.262" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98/answer" :answer-field/id #uuid "546450ba-f0fc-5ac8-a380-753b82559f9e" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-98/answer/f8c741b26d6c252fd277bcaeae6e7c3326f626b9a3e0f43d8fd01cd3ffaa30e0" :answer-field/choices ["q-98/answer/f8c741b26d6c252fd277bcaeae6e7c3326f626b9a3e0f43d8fd01cd3ffaa30e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98" :question/id #uuid "4bb0c190-0bc7-5c24-bdb9-2ae5232df4b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-98" :question/problem "Use a calculator to evaluate ${log}_{12}(23)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's calculate ${log}_{12}(23)$ by changing the base $12$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}X=\\frac{{log}_{b}X}{{log}_{b}a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=12,$ $X=23,$ $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{12}(23) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}(23)}{{log}_{10}(12)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}(23)}{\\operatorname{log}(12)} \\\\  & \\approx \\frac{1.361\\,728}{1.079\\,181} \\\\  & \\approx 1.262\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-98/answer"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bccd26ff-1dc5-5817-962b-a1ef1f46b2fb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70908/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "821db7a8-8f56-556d-9121-149c04644e3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70908/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "7550839f-4794-5b19-970d-ea559dd47bd0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70908/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "038d8bbc-19ca-5980-b57c-1bfecd77321c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70908/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "4f77c179-e69a-59bd-9aee